{"text": "2085196590\n\nKelley, Loren L.\n\nKelley, Loven L.\n\u2018Thursday, November 15, 2001 5:55 PM\namc Bradley E-mail)\nGroataus, Steve (Leo Burnet); Codeta, Marge E.; Rush, Sonya C; Clagget, Tom (Leo\nurn\nSubjoct: Request for Data 11/15\n\nGarrick,\n\u2018Some additional Requests for Data came out from the meeting today. | have attempted to put together\n\"straw dogs\" of what we'd like to see. There are three tabs in the attached spreadsheet.\n\n1) Non-Responders 30)+-\nFor Marlboro, Parliament, Slims and Basic, we need this chart populated. We are looking at the number of\n\u2018opportunities Non-Responders have been given to respond over the past 24 months. We do NOT want to\ninclude equity mailings in this analysis. Can you limit it to only response vehicles? Marlboro is the priority, if\ntime prohibits you from pulling this information for the other three brands.\n\n2) Doral Smokers\nThere is question as to whether or not it makes sense to use \u201cany response\" in allocating Discount\nsmokers. What if a Doral Smoker received 6 mailings from Basic and responded to 5 of them and also\nreceived 1 mailing from Marlboro and responded to that. In the \"any response* scenario, that Doral\n\u2018Smoker would be allocated to Marlboro. Is that the right thing to do.\n\nWe want to look at the number of \u201copportunities\u201d a Doral smoker was given to respond to Marlboro and\nwhether or not he responded. Same exercise for Basic,\n\n| believe we would limit the population to only those Doral smokers who have responded to both Marlboro\nand Basic in the last 12 months, but we need to confirm that.\n\n3) Discount Smokers (less Doral)\nSame as above.\n\n\u2018We will discuss this during the status call at 10am ET on Friday. We can hash things out then, Talk to you\nthen,\n\ni)\n\n\u2018Alcationt1_15Req\nstage\n\nLoren\n\n917-663-2351\n\u2018917-863-5236 FAX",
"words": [
